  "prefLabel": "We 602.06 Well Location: Protective Well Radii, Generally",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "We 602.06 Well Location: Protective Well Radii, Generally.\n\n(a) Wells shall be located to reduce the likelihood of contamination from sources of pollution at or near the ground surface.\n\n(b) As specified in Env-Wq 1008.06, a protective area designated as the protective well radius shall be maintained around every private commercial or non-commercial drinking water well.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for We 600) #12083 eff 3-1-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/we100-1000.html"
